Assertions:
[ERRORS label=create_org] errors[] empty {OBSERVED}
[BLADE] BASELINE_OPTIONS includes 'Purchasing agent' {OBSERVED} -- proves the picker is governed by the STORE-scope override (@td(B2B_STORE_MEMBERSHIP_ROLES.seeded_values)), NOT by the GLOBAL control value just written ([Organization maintainer] alone would not include it) -- store wins regardless of global {BL}
[BLADE] BASELINE_OPTIONS also includes 'Sales Representative' {OBSERVED} -- a role outside the module's hardcoded pool, present only via the STORE override; confirms the picker reads the live STORE tenant value, not the descriptor pool's AllowedValues literal {BL}
[BLADE] AFTER_NARROW_OPTIONS does NOT include @td(B2B_STORE_MEMBERSHIP_ROLES.narrowed_omitted_role) {OBSERVED} -- narrowing the STORE value to @td(B2B_STORE_MEMBERSHIP_ROLES.narrowed_values) removed a role that was genuinely visible in BASELINE_OPTIONS, not one added speculatively {BL}
[BLADE] AFTER_NARROW_OPTIONS does not equal the GLOBAL control set ([Organization maintainer] only) either -- e.g. 'Organization employee' remains present {OBSERVED} -- confirms the picker keeps reading the STORE value throughout and never falls back to GLOBAL while STORE is non-empty, even a single-entry STORE value {BL}

[ERRORS label=create_org] errors[] empty {OBSERVED}
[BLADE] EXPECTED_GLOBAL == {Organization maintainer, Purchasing agent} {OBSERVED} -- read back live from read_global in this same run, never assumed {BL}
[BLADE] BASELINE_UNKEYWORDED_OPTIONS includes 'Purchasing agent' {OBSERVED} -- a member of EXPECTED_GLOBAL, confirming the picker fell through to GLOBAL rather than showing zero options {BL}
[BLADE] BASELINE_UNKEYWORDED_OPTIONS does NOT include 'Advanced Sales Representative' {OBSERVED} -- part of the STORE fixture (@td(B2B_STORE_MEMBERSHIP_ROLES.sales_rep_roles)) but not of EXPECTED_GLOBAL; its absence rules out the picker still serving the stale STORE fixture value {BL}
[BLADE] KEYWORD_MAINTAINER_OPTIONS includes 'Organization maintainer' {OBSERVED} -- the second EXPECTED_GLOBAL entry, confirmed present once the picker's default-page paging is accounted for via keyword {BL}
[BLADE] KEYWORD_EMPLOYEE_OPTIONS does NOT include 'Organization employee' {OBSERVED} -- absent from EXPECTED_GLOBAL; its absence even WITH a keyword bringing it into scope rules out paging as the explanation and isolates a genuine filter result, not an unconditional 'empty STORE = all roles' fallback {BL}
